    "narrative": "The analytical outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP favors the top of the order tonight, with **James Wood** serving as our clear offensive anchor. Facing Kyle Freeland in a hitter-friendly environment, **James Wood** boasts a stellar 72.71 score, bolstered by an elite 0.430 xwOBA and a +14% park factor, making him our highest-projected contributor for Runs and HRs. Similarly, **Tyler Soderstrom** offers immense value at 66.96, taking advantage of a favorable matchup against Bratt\u2019s 7.04 xERA. We are also leaning heavily into the platoon advantage for **Brice Turang** and **Isaac Paredes**; both project well into the 64-range, as their ability to exploit matchup-specific strengths in the 3-hole provides a steady floor for our AVG and RBI categories. \n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Austin Riley** on the bench despite his solid 63.08 projection. While **Austin Riley** remains a reliable asset, the high-efficiency scores of **Gabriel Moreno** and **Josh Naylor**\u2014who are both positioned to capitalize on matchups against subpar starters like Springs and Abbott\u2014narrowly edged him out of the starting nine. We are also exercising caution with **Jose Caballero** and **Zach McKinstry**; while their utility in stolen base attempts is vital to our team identity, their lower raw scores reflect the risk of facing efficient opposing pitchers. We remain vigilant regarding **Travis Bazzana**, whose 42.65 score is suppressed by the presence of Pablo Lopez, and **Edwin Arroyo**, whose sub-40 score necessitates a seat on the bench to preserve our critical game caps as we navigate the remainder of the 2026 season.",
